    ],
    "justification": "The lemma separates the observable frontier used to choose a temperature from the oracle regret path that the confidence envelope covers.",
    "gap": "Post-search arguments such as Kang's assume an observed indexed statistic, while the causal regret here contains an unobserved oracle comparator; the exact event inclusion supplies the needed operational bridge without a false plug-in equality.",
    "consumer": "A planner can compute a temperature from the displayed plug-in frontier and invoke the simultaneous oracle-regret certificate at precisely that observed-data choice.",
    "proof_tex": "Every cell count and cell sum in \\(\\widehat\\mu_{n,ja}\\) is\n\\(\\mathcal F_n^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)-measurable.  The empty-cell convention is\ndeterministic, so \\(\\widehat\\Delta_n\\), \\(\\widehat u_n\\), and\n\\(\\widehat p_n\\) are measurable with respect to that sigma-field.  For fixed\nfinite \\(c>0\\), the exponential and logarithm formulas defining the plug-in\nfrontier are continuous functions of these finitely many statistics.  The\nhard endpoint is Borel because it is formed from finitely many maxima, and\nthe quadratic endpoint is continuous.  The endpoint estimates (19) and\n(23), applied with \\(\\widehat u_n\\), show that each realized plug-in path is\ncontinuous.  Separability of \\(C([0,1])\\) then shows that\n\\(\\widehat{\\mathfrak F}_n\\) is a\n\\(\\mathcal F_n^{\\mathrm{obs}}\\)-measurable random element.  Its displayed\nformula uses only the observed triples, the supplied benchmark \\(b\\), and\nthe declared cell estimators; in particular it nowhere uses\n\\(\\Delta_n,u_n\\), or \\(E_n\\).\n\nFor every function \\(f\\in C([0,1])\\), every \\(s\\in[0,1]\\), and every real\n\\(x\\), the deterministic implication\n\\[\n \\sup_{t\\in[0,1]}f(t)\\le x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad f(s)\\le x           \\tag{29}\n\\]\nholds.  Apply (29) pointwise with \\(f=T_n\\) and\n\\(s=\\widehat t_n\\).  Measurability of the selector is needed only to make\nthe right-hand event measurable; no independence is used.  This proves\n\\[\n \\{\\sup_tT_n(t)\\le x\\}\\subseteq\\{T_n(\\widehat t_n)\\le x\\}.              \\tag{30}\n\\]\nOn \\(0<\\widehat t_n<1\\), put\n\\(\\widehat c_n=\\widehat t_n/(1-\\widehat t_n)\\).  The exact identity in\n\\(\\mathrm{lem:exact\\mbox{-}regret\\mbox{-}path}\\), evaluated at the\nrealized positive value \\(\\widehat c_n\\), gives\n\\[\n T_n(\\widehat t_n)\n =(1+\\widehat c_n)\\sqrt n\\,\\mathscr R_n(\\widehat c_n).                 \\tag{31}\n\\]\nEquations (30)--(31) prove the bridge and also show why no equality between\nthe observable frontier and the oracle regret path is required.",
